Z||000006||Alex4mula||11-28-2001||03:34 PM||||Thanks all  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> To be honest with you I like the Viper/Vette etc. Yellow. Is my wife who want's something more subtle if you can call yellow that.<BR>The problem I have with the chip books is that the sample is very small. I choosed the red in my car that way and came out brighter than I thought. Lucky was OK for me.<BR>I saw a yellow Saturn but was not sure if is the latest. The one I saw was a yellow very similar to the Fiero yellow or lighter.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||11-28-2001||03:37 PM||||Be careful, as yellow can be a difficult color to choose.  Especially out of a chip book!  If you get the wrong shade everyone will think you drive a school bus yellow Fiero.<P>The Aztek has a bus yellow option.  I like the Mustang yellow, and the Cougar yellow (probably the same color) its not overly bright, but not nearly as muted as the original Fiero yellow.  The Saturn coupes also have a nice yellow.||||reg||1
